---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How NoCharge handles analytics, advertising, and data stored on your device."
  path="/privacy/"
  showAds={false}
>
  <article class="privacy">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">← Home</a>
    <header>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">The short version: no accounts, and game data stays on your device.</p>
      <p class="privacy__updated">Last updated: August 17, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy__body panel">
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-choices">
        <h2 id="privacy-choices">Your privacy choices</h2>
        <p>
          Analytics and advertising are off by default. They load only after you allow their categories. You can
          review or withdraw that choice at any time; necessary storage remains available for this choice and
          local game features.
        </p>
        <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-consent-open>Review privacy choices</button>
        <p class="privacy__status" data-consent-summary aria-live="polite">Loading your current choices…</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="local-data">
        <h2 id="local-data">Data on your device</h2>
        <p>
          NoCharge uses your browser’s local storage for high scores, game preferences, and your shared sound
          preference. That information is not sent to NoCharge and remains until you clear it in your browser or
          use the button below.
        </p>
        <p>
          Clear game data removes local scores, game preferences, and the shared sound preference. It does not
          remove your privacy or consent choice, which stays saved so analytics and advertising remain exactly as
          you left them.
        </p>
        <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-clear-games>Clear game data</button>
        <p class="privacy__status" data-game-status aria-live="polite"></p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="analytics">
        <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          If you allow analytics, NoCharge loads Google Analytics to understand broad usage such as page visits
          and device types. We request IP anonymization, but your browser still connects directly to Google and
          Google may use browser identifiers or cookies. The tag is not requested when analytics is off. See the
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>. With analytics consent, NoCharge may also
          send a privacy-limited technical exception category to this same analytics path to help identify site errors.
          It does not send game selections, Word Tile Rush words, form text, local storage, URL queries, or fragments.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="advertising">
        <h2 id="advertising">Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          If you allow advertising, NoCharge loads sandboxed banner ads supplied by Adsterra on the home and
          game pages. Your browser then connects directly to the advertising provider. The provider may receive
          technical data such as your IP address, browser and device details, the referring site, and ad
          interactions, and may use cookies or similar identifiers. No ad frame or Adsterra script is requested
          while advertising is off. Read Adsterra’s
          <a href="https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy-managed/">Privacy Policy</a> and
          <a href="https://adsterra.com/cookies/">Cookies Policy</a> for its practices and controls.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a banner does not fill, NoCharge may show a clearly labeled sponsored link using Adsterra’s
          provider-controlled anti-adblock domain. It remains hidden until advertising is allowed and opens only
          after you select it. NoCharge does not place popups or full-screen interstitials over gameplay.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="accounts-retention">
        <h2 id="accounts-retention">Accounts and retention</h2>
        <p>
          NoCharge has no user accounts, passwords, or database of player scores. Local game data remains on
          your device until you remove it. Google and Adsterra control retention for information they process
          under their own policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact">
        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          This site is intended for users 13 and older. For privacy questions or requests, email
          <a href="mailto:hello@nocharge.net">hello@nocharge.net</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const clearGames = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-clear-games]');
  const gameStatus = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-game-status]');

  clearGames?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    try {
      // Explicit allowlist of current game-only keys. The privacy/consent key is
      // intentionally omitted so clearing game data never touches the consent
      // choice, its categories, timestamp, or schema version. Unrelated origin
      // storage is left untouched.
      const gameScoreIds = ['memory-match', 'word-tile-rush', 'color-flip', 'color-flip-turn-based'];
      const gamePreferenceKeys = ['game-muted'];
      const gameKeys = [
        ...gameScoreIds.map((id) => `nocharge:${id}:high`),
        'nocharge:memory-match:best-moves',
        ...gamePreferenceKeys.map((pref) => `nocharge:pref:${pref}`),
      ];
      gameKeys.forEach((key) => localStorage.removeItem(key));
      if (gameStatus) gameStatus.textContent = 'Game scores and preferences were cleared from this browser.';
    } catch {
      if (gameStatus) gameStatus.textContent = 'This browser did not allow game data to be cleared.';
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  .privacy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .privacy__updated {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .privacy__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.3rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .privacy__body section {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .privacy__body section + section {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .privacy__body h2 {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .privacy__body p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .privacy__body a {
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .privacy__status {
    min-height: 1.3rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>
